# tally 2.1.8 S8 (#181), E §10 Long derivations fold: "A cause met again is referenced by its line, once under each
# line that reads it". f reads x twice and g reads f and x twice: x prints in full under f's rule, once, and is
# referenced once under g's. 2.1.7's refcore (and the M2 engine) printed a reference for each read: one more under
# f's rule, two under g's.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input x: money PLN
input y: money PLN

def f: money PLN
  rule base = x + x + y

def g: money PLN
  rule base = f + x + x

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x = 10.00 PLN "s"
  y = 1.00 PLN "s"

ask e: explain g
=== expect
e: 41.00 PLN
  [1] g = 41.00 PLN
      rule base: won
        [2] f = 21.00 PLN
            rule base: won
              [3] row v:x = 10.00 PLN
                  version v, source s, "s", locator "s", governs always, known 2026-01-01
              [4] row v:y = 1.00 PLN
                  version v, source s, "s", locator "s", governs always, known 2026-01-01
        (v:x: see [3])
  cut 2026-03-01
